{
  "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted. Define the actual closed conditional-mean-zero space H_perp=ker P in L²(J;ℝ), with its inherited complete Hilbert structure; this is not merely the globally zero-mean joint space. There exists B_0:H_P^0→H_perp whose inclusion equals B i_0. There exists V_0:H_P^0→H_perp with V_0=B_0 Inv, B_0=V_0 Γ_0, V_0* V_0=I and ‖V_0 f‖=‖f‖ for every f∈H_P^0. All these objects and identities are conclusions from the same original inputs. There exists the canonical bounded residual map R:L²(J;ℝ)→H_perp with i_perp Rg=g−Pg for every joint g. The SAME ambient adjoint satisfies B* g=i_0 B_0* Rg for every joint g; the printed intrinsic block adjoint is recovered on H_perp. For every actual joint f∈L²(J;ℝ) with ∫f dJ=0, there exists f_P∈H_P^0 whose inclusion is E[f|Y]. Put f_perp=Rf and f_V=V_0* f_perp∈the SAME H_P^0. Then B* i_perp f_perp=i_0 Γ_0 f_V=Γ_P i_0 f_V, ‖f‖²=‖f_P‖²+‖f_perp‖² and ‖f_V‖≤‖f_perp‖. The genuine original-input Test derives f=i i_0 f_P+i_perp f_perp, B* f=Γ_P i_0 f_V and ‖f_V‖²≤‖f‖²−‖f_P‖². The global zero-mean condition is a quantified input restriction to this concluded implication, not an extra assumption on the potential or an operator certificate. One private proposition definition per file stores exactly the original full statement solely to stage dependent elaboration; it assumes and proves no mathematics. No onto/coisometry,full modified-energy bound or later dynamics/cost/composition result is asserted.",
  "paper_assumptions": [
    "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel base E with canonical volume, including the disclosed rank-zero extension; V is C²; 0<α≤β; both global Hessian bounds; η>0 and βη≤1.",
    "Canonical normalized laws/kernel, onto pullback e, SAME U/T, full and centered roots, exact centering, gap, unit and bounded inverse are conclusions. Conditional actions are per-observable AE. L² is not assumed finite-dimensional.",
    "γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη); the inverse acts only on H_P^0=ker⟨e1,·⟩ with inherited Hilbert structure; the legal endpoint αη=1 is retained.",
    "H_perp is exactly ker P (conditional expectation given Y), while H_P^0 is the zero ν-mean macroscopic space. Their complete Hilbert structures, B_0 and V_0 are internally constructed; no onto-kerP or coisometry assumption is introduced.",
    "The concluded global-input implication quantifies every f∈L²(J) with integral zero. R,conditional centering,constant annihilation,adjoint range and norm decomposition are derived internally. Private statement definitions expand literally to the original sealed propositions and add no premise."
  ],
  "route_boundary": "Original C2/two Hessians/positive capped eta only,rank0/alphaeta1 retained. All constant-annihilation/adjoint range/centering/projection/complete structures are internal. This is the actual-input domain adapter and first-corrector geometry; no full B20 bound,root commutation/B21,halfturn,H1/operator inequalities,dynamics/main/errors/expected-query-cost/actual-input composition,onto or reverse-product claim.",
  "units": [
    {
      "title": "Actual ambient adjoint and globally centered corrector",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Keep the actual spaces and construct the conditional residual",
          "text": "Reuse the SAME actual65 laws,normalized conditional kernel,reflection,root,inverse and polar witnesses. P is conditional expectation given Y. Idempotence gives P(g−Pg)=0, so the canonical bounded map R has exact codomain ker P; R is identity there.",
          "formula": "Rg=g-Pg\\in\\ker P,\\quad R i_\\perp=I_{\\ker P}.",
          "lean": "  classical\n  dsimp only\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) := ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n  let HP := lpMeas ℝ ℝ mY 2 J\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP := HP.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP := HP.innerProductSpace\n  let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    HP.subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ := J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n  have hBase := AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.PolarIsometry.actual_centered_polar_isometry\n    (E:=E) (V:=V) (α:=α) (β:=β) (η:=η) hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  dsimp only at hBase\n  rcases hBase with\n    ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,\n      T,hTs,hAll,hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,\n      q,hqa,hTq,hq,hCenter,hΓPq,hγ,ΓP0,hΓP0,hPos0,hOrder0,hUnit,\n      Inv,hLeft,hRight,hNormInv,B0,hB0,V0,hVdef,hFactor,hVadj,hVnorm⟩\n  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP := HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  let qP : HP := e q\n  let HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP0 := HP0.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP0 := HP0.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  let Hperp := P.ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup Hperp := Hperp.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ Hperp := Hperp.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace Hperp := P.isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  change HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp at B0 V0\n  change HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 at ΓP0 Inv\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure J := hJ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure ν := hν\n  let C : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] HP := condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ:=J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n  have hPself (g k : Lp ℝ 2 J) : inner ℝ (P g) k=inner ℝ g (P k) :=\n    inner_condExpL2_left_eq_right measurable_snd.comap_le\n  have hPid (g : Lp ℝ 2 J) : P (P g)=P g := hPf (C g)\n  let R : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Hperp :=\n    ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P).codRestrict Hperp (by\n      intro g\n      change P (g-P g)=0\n      rw [map_sub,hPid,sub_self])\n  have hR (g : Lp ℝ 2 J) : (R g : Lp ℝ 2 J)=g-P g := rfl\n  have hRself (g : Hperp) : R (g : Lp ℝ 2 J)=g := by\n    apply Subtype.ext\n    change (g : Lp ℝ 2 J)-P g=g\n    rw [show P (g : Lp ℝ 2 J)=0 from g.property,sub_zero]\n",
          "detail": "Literal compiled BODY excerpt; exact preceding local definitions/derived facts remain in scope. Private statement definition is fully included in reviewed module text and source download.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/AmbientAdjointCorrector.lean",
